      "body": "## Finding description\nAave’s new **Merit Rewards program** distributes incentives via a **Merkle-based claim system** (through [Merkl](https://app.merkl.xyz)) instead of the standard `RewardsController`.\n\nAccording to aave documentation:\n\n>Merit Program Merit is an Aave-alignment user reward system, designed as a merkle-tree-based periodic airdrop to incentivise Aave-aligned behaviours and enhance the competitiveness of the Aave protocol. More information and interface to access merit distribution can be found [here](https://apps.aavechan.com/merit).\n\nCurrently, `Distributor::claimAaveRewards()` only calls:\n\n```solidity\nIRewardsController(aaveRewardsController).claimRewards(...)\n```\n\nand does not account for Merit rewards, which would need to call `Claim()` on `Angle Protocol: Distributor`.\n\nAs a result, users may **miss out on unclaimed Merit rewards**, which expire after **6 months**, leading to permanent loss. Since users could reasonably assume all rewards are handled by `claimAaveRewards()`, this creates a usability and value loss risk.\n### Severity\n\n- **Impact: Medium** — Users can permanently lose rewards.\n- **Likelihood: Medium** — Merit campaigns are active and many users qualify.\n### Recommendation\n\nExtend `Distributor::claimAaveRewards()` to also claim **Merit rewards** via the Merkle interface, preventing users from unknowingly forfeiting them.",
      "proofOfConcept": "Please note this POC is via foundry. It uses a rudimentary approach by having a mock MeritRewards, as it is difficult to write a POC for a feature that doesn't exist. It shows that the `Distributor::claimAaveRewards()` function only claims rewards via the `aaveRewardsController`, not anywhere else, forfeiting any merkl rewards, which will become permanently lost after 6 months.\n\nTo setup foundry in the project, execute the following commands \n\n```\nforge init . --force\nforge install openzeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts\nforge build\n```\n\nin `foundry.toml`, add the following line \n\n`test = 'testFoundry'`\n\nIn the root of the project, create a new folder called `2025-08-morpheus/testFoundry` and add the following test into a file named `Distributor.t.sol`, and run the following command `forge test --mt test_claimAaveRewards_doesNotClaimMerit`\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.20;\n\nimport \"../lib/forge-std/src/Test.sol\";\n\n// contracts\nimport {Distributor} from \"../contracts/capital-protocol/Distributor.sol\";\nimport {AavePoolMock} from \"../contracts/mock/capital-protocol/aave/AavePoolMock.sol\";\nimport {AavePoolDataProviderMock} from \"../contracts/mock/capital-protocol/aave/AavePoolDataProviderMock.sol\";\nimport {RewardPoolMock} from \"../contracts/mock/capital-protocol/RewardPoolMock.sol\";\nimport {L1SenderMock} from \"../contracts/mock/capital-protocol/L1SenderMock.sol\";\nimport {ChainLinkDataConsumerMock} from \"../contracts/mock/capital-protocol/chainlink/ChainLinkDataConsumerMock.sol\";\nimport {DepositPoolMock} from \"../contracts/mock/capital-protocol/DepositPoolMock.sol\";\nimport {ERC20Token} from \"../contracts/mock/tokens/ERC20Token.sol\";\n\n// proxy\nimport {ERC1967Proxy} from \"../lib/openzeppelin-contracts/contracts/proxy/ERC1967/ERC1967Proxy.sol\";\n\ncontract DistributorTest is Test {\n    enum Strategy {\n        NONE,\n        NO_YIELD,\n        AAVE\n    }\n\n    struct DepositPoolTestOnlyInfo {\n        uint256 rewardPoolId;\n        string chainLinkPath;\n        uint256 chainLinkPrice;\n        ERC20Token depositToken;\n        DepositPoolMock depositPool;\n        ERC20Token aToken;\n        Strategy strategy;\n    }\n\n    address OWNER;\n    address BOB;\n\n    Distributor distributor;\n    ChainLinkDataConsumerMock chainLinkDataConsumerMock;\n    AavePoolDataProviderMock aavePoolDataProviderMock;\n    AavePoolMock aavePoolMock;\n    RewardPoolMock rewardPoolMock;\n    L1SenderMock l1SenderMock;\n\n    DepositPoolTestOnlyInfo dp0Info;\n    DepositPoolTestOnlyInfo dp1Info;\n    DepositPoolTestOnlyInfo dp2Info;\n    DepositPoolTestOnlyInfo[] depositPools;\n    MeritRewardsMock meritRewardsMock;\n\n    uint256 publicRewardPoolId = 0;\n    uint256 privateRewardPoolId = 1;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        // Addresses\n        OWNER = makeAddr(\"OWNER\");\n        BOB = makeAddr(\"BOB\");\n\n        // deploy mocks\n        chainLinkDataConsumerMock = new ChainLinkDataConsumerMock();\n        aavePoolDataProviderMock = new AavePoolDataProviderMock();\n        aavePoolMock = new AavePoolMock(address(aavePoolDataProviderMock));\n        rewardPoolMock = new RewardPoolMock();\n        l1SenderMock = new L1SenderMock();\n\n        // deploy implementation and proxy\n        Distributor impl = new Distributor();\n        ERC1967Proxy proxy = new ERC1967Proxy(\n            address(impl),\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(\n                Distributor.Distributor_init.selector,\n                address(chainLinkDataConsumerMock),\n                address(aavePoolMock),\n                address(aavePoolDataProviderMock),\n                address(rewardPoolMock),\n                address(l1SenderMock)\n            )\n        );\n        distributor = Distributor(address(proxy));\n\n        // deploy Merit mock\n        meritRewardsMock = new MeritRewardsMock();\n\n        // deploy Aave reward controller and set it **after proxy is ready**\n        RewardControllerMock aaveRewardsControllerMock = new RewardControllerMock();\n        vm.prank(distributor.owner()); // simulate onlyOwner\n        distributor.setAaveRewardsController(address(aaveRewardsControllerMock));\n\n        // setup tokens + pools\n        ERC20Token depositToken1 = new ERC20Token();\n        ERC20Token depositToken2 = new ERC20Token();\n\n        DepositPoolMock depositPool1 = new DepositPoolMock(address(distributor), address(depositToken1));\n        DepositPoolMock depositPool2 = new DepositPoolMock(address(distributor), address(depositToken2));\n\n        dp0Info = DepositPoolTestOnlyInfo({\n            rewardPoolId: publicRewardPoolId,\n            chainLinkPath: \"wETH/USD\",\n            chainLinkPrice: 0,\n            depositToken: depositToken1,\n            depositPool: depositPool1,\n            aToken: new ERC20Token(),\n            strategy: Strategy.NONE\n        });\n\n        dp1Info = DepositPoolTestOnlyInfo({\n            rewardPoolId: publicRewardPoolId,\n            chainLinkPath: \"cbBTC/USD\",\n            chainLinkPrice: 0,\n            depositToken: depositToken2,\n            depositPool: depositPool2,\n            aToken: new ERC20Token(),\n            strategy: Strategy.AAVE\n        });\n\n        dp2Info = DepositPoolTestOnlyInfo({\n            rewardPoolId: privateRewardPoolId,\n            chainLinkPath: \"---\",\n            chainLinkPrice: 0,\n            depositToken: depositToken1,\n            depositPool: depositPool1,\n            aToken: new ERC20Token(),\n            strategy: Strategy.NO_YIELD\n        });\n\n        depositPools.push(dp0Info);\n        depositPools.push(dp1Info);\n        depositPools.push(dp2Info);\n\n        // wire aToken addresses in the mock\n        aavePoolDataProviderMock.setATokenAddress(address(dp1Info.depositToken), address(dp1Info.aToken));\n\n        // setup reward pools in mock\n        rewardPoolMock.setIsRewardPoolExist(publicRewardPoolId, true);\n        rewardPoolMock.setIsRewardPoolExist(privateRewardPoolId, true);\n        rewardPoolMock.setIsRewardPoolPublic(publicRewardPoolId, true);\n\n        // set token decimals\n        depositToken1.setDecimals(6);\n    }\n\n    function test_claimAaveRewards_doesNotClaimMerit() public {\n        address[] memory assets = new address[](2);\n        assets[0] = address(dp1Info.aToken);\n\n        uint256 amount = 1000;\n        address to = BOB;\n        address reward = address(rewardPoolMock);\n\n        // simulate OWNER claiming Aave rewards\n        vm.prank(distributor.owner());\n        distributor.claimAaveRewards(assets, amount, to, reward);\n\n        // Merit rewards should remain untouched\n        assertEq(meritRewardsMock.lastClaimer(), address(0), \"Merit rewards should not be claimed yet\");\n    }\n}\n\n// Mocks\ncontract RewardControllerMock {\n    bool public claimed = false;\n    uint256 public lastClaimedAmount;\n\n    function claimRewards(address[] calldata assets, uint256 amount, address to, address reward)\n        external\n        returns (uint256)\n    {\n        require(to != address(0), \"invalid recipient\"); // mimic safety check\n        require(assets.length > 0, \"no assets\"); // mimic safety check\n\n        claimed = true;\n        lastClaimedAmount = amount;\n\n        return amount; // must return a uint256, or the Distributor call will revert\n    }\n}\n\ncontract MeritRewardsMock {\n    address public lastClaimer;\n\n    function claim(address user, uint256 amount, bytes32[] calldata proof) external {\n        lastClaimer = user;\n    }\n}\n```",
